<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Demetrius of Pharos</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 214 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Demetrius of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hvar">Pharos</a> was a Greek ruler of the Adriatic island of Pharos who served the Illyrian queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teuta">Teuta</a> and then went over to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in the First Illyrian War of 229 BCE, receiving a domain on the coast. His later raids and alliance with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a> provoked the Second Illyrian War of 219 BCE, in which Rome drove him out. He fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-v-of-macedon">Philip V of Macedon</a> and was killed attacking Messene in 214 BCE.</p></div>
